;smartlock_v2_beta_3_1
;Oj742
;
;A lock that checks polarity cycle and offset of the opponent to create an accurate lock
;It also skips clearing spaces where there is nothing
;
;Taking a page from omnipotence's book we have special casing
;for certain programs, though it is hopefully more generalized and less exploitable
;It uses a decoy instead of a flag for locking in some hope that it won't completely die against timer clears
;
;Side note: OHGODWHATAMIDOINGIHAVENOIDEAPLEASEHELP

>(+)*5>->+>->->(+)*5<<(-)*13<(+)*6<(-)*13<(+)*17>>>>>(>[-[++[+[+[-----[-[(>)*1(>[+[--[-[-[+++++[+[([(-)*120[-]]>)*2([(+)*39[-]]>)*3([(+)*65[-]]>)*3([(+)*100[+]]>)*6]]]]]]])*21
]]]]]]]+)*2(<)*5([{
;we've been waiting for some sort of enemy contact for 6250 cycles now so assume that the opponent is defensive or really really slow
;
;why 6250 cycles? its a number likely greater than the number of cycles it should take to detect an offensive program and it seems
;to be the magic number for racking up the most points against ais523_preparation

;Anti defence program code derived from Oj742_smart_timerclear
(>)*5(>[-[++[+[+[-----[-[(+)*14<<[(+)*11[-]]]]]]]]>][++[+.]]>
([-{[(+)*90[+.]]}>[-[++[+[+[-----[-[(+)*24<<[-]]]]]]]>][++[+.]]>
